From: Diego Chagas <drochachagas@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:44:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Properties panel: Transform, Align and Distribute, Quick
 Actions

Photoshop's Properties panel as a dockable (gimp-properties-editor,
Windows > Dockable Dialogs > Properties). For the selected layers:

- the layer's kind (Pixel Layer, Text Layer, Smart Object, Shape Layer,
  Layer Group, or how many layers);
- Transform, for one layer: W and H (linked: the aspect ratio kept, the
  top-left corner staying), X and Y, a rotation angle (the layer is
  rotated about its centre and the field goes back to 0, as Photoshop's
  for pixel layers), flip horizontally / vertically; locked position or
  contents make the fields insensitive; with several layers the
  fields show, read-only, the box around their pixels;
- Align and Distribute: one layer to the canvas, several to the box around
  their non-empty pixels, as Photoshop; distribute (3 layers or more) is
  GIMP's own even-gap distribution;
- Quick Actions: Remove Background and Select Subject, buttons running the
  GIMPhoto plug-in procedures gimphoto-remove-background and
  gimphoto-select-subject, insensitive until those plug-ins exist.

Each button or edit is one undo step. The panel follows the image's
selected layers and its undo events.

